{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1037353-the-necromancy-homebrew-thread","id":1037353,"title":"The Necromancy Homebrew Thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-24T12:15:57-08:00","id":1037353,"title":"The Necromancy Homebrew Thread","content":"<b>(Deleted because reasons)</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":482,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","user":"Ekorren","date":". 08-14-2018, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T12:35:46-08:00","id":1040815,"title":"","content":"Okay! Will offer some comments.<br /> <br /> <b>The Three Circles</b><ul><li>Second paragraph states that a necromancer begins by learning Labyrinth Circle Necromancy, when this is not true, they begin by learning Shadowlands Circle Necromancy.</li> <li>I might suggest removing mention of the Liminals here, or possibly giving them access to Labyrinth Circle Necromancy. I believe we've been informed that their level of ability is Terrestrial going on low Celestial in some ways, and if there were any place where they might go further, I would suggest that it be there.</li> </ul><b>Banishing Ghosts</b><ul><li>I'm not sure I'd give this as an intrinsic capability. Banishing spells are generally gone and I think that's probably a good thing. It might be worth inquiring around or thinking about why it's strictly necessary for them to have this capability as an intrinsic one, if not as an actual spell.</li> </ul><b>Anointed by Crimson</b><ul><li>While I originally wrote it, the descriptive text of this Initiation definitely needs punching up, IMO. The language is awkward and repetitive.</li> <li>I like that first shaping ritual. Clever way to do it.</li> <li>The second one is crazy good. Although the amount of blood required makes it not super feasible beyond certain levels of usage, but this one is very powerful, and that might be something to look out for. Also what happens if you bathe in the blood of a Size 0 group of people? That is, 1-2 people or a group of sub-size 1 people?</li> <li>The language of this last one should be changed. Rather than saying it lowers the cost, I would say they gain necrosis. I would also describe the nature of the kinds of stunts which would qualify for this shaping ritual.</li> </ul><b>Madness of the Labyrinth</b><ul><li>This first shaping ritual is taken from the Nephwrack QC, and might be a little too powerful. I would suggest replacing that 10 with different values, like Essence + Intelligence (Incidentally, this would likely give you the equivalent to what the Nephwrack gets at Essence 5/Intelligence 5) which might help balance it more.</li> <li>The second one, I might suggest including qualifying statements about this only working on living battlegroups and an upper limit on how much necrosis you can gain from damaging one of them per attack.</li> <li>I think you rebalanced Void-Eaten Soul, but I'm not sure. I still think this is a bit <i>too </i>good.</li> </ul><b>Schooling of the Maze</b><ul><li>I might suggest rewriting the fluff of this one to cast it as the &quot;Sijanese Initiation&quot; y'know, one involving the Funereal Order.</li> </ul>On to some Spell thoughts!\u200b<br /> <br /> <b>Black Candle Visage</b><ul><li>This feels exactly like the kind of spell that wouldn't appear in 3e but was in previous editions because we didn't have sorcerous/necromantic workings to use.</li> <li>If you absolutely have to keep it, I would simplify it with the suggestion that it simply allows you to twist normal or mundane ghosts into more monstrous varieties. Like Tiger Warrior Training turning Medium Infantry into Elite Troops, this could turn a Haunt or an Honored Ancestor or a Hungry Ghost or a War Ghost into a Mortwright for example. I'd probably pick a few simple templates of ghostly monstrousness (Or just stick to mortwrights) to facilitate this.</li> <li>I critique the use of the Crafts system here not because I don't like it (I do!) but because I think it's easy to systemize this kind of thing (only 1 dot merits, only 2 dot merits, etc.) to the point of uselessness. If I had to use Crafts with this, I would suggest that minor alterations to the ghost might be minor projects, while severe ones which reshape the form or alter the abilities would be Major. Keeping it simple so that it's easy to use in play.</li> </ul><b>Bless the Rapine Soul</b><ul><li>Interesting! I like this one. I have a kind of intangible weird feeling about it, but I like it. I think it could use some better word ordering or simplification, hmm.</li> <li>Why the Mute keyword?</li> <li>I think this makes sense as using the default number of necrosis/smotes needed to cast the spell at 15, rather than 10.</li> </ul><b>Blessed Dead Fools</b><ul><li>Two bless spells in a row! I'd consider some name fiddling.</li> <li>I appreciate the flavor of this one, but question the necessity of its existence. Since this is a digital work and wordcount isn't a problem, it's less bothersome, but if this were being made to be printed, I would cut this in favor of more useful spells.</li> </ul><b>Blood Lash</b><ul><li>Cool. I suggest ditching the 2 dot merit for Anointed by Crimson if you want this spell, as that way it isn't a redundancy for the redundant department of redundancy to deal with.</li> <li>I think having people have to reference back to the corebook to figure out what the heck stats their blood lash gets is not a good call. I'd follow the model of Wood Dragon's Claws, which describes the traits of the weapon and what it might be used for inside. the body text.</li> <li>It's interesting that this costs 2wp. WDC costs 1wp and you're getting roughly similar value from them.</li> <li>I caution against having it inflict a second health level of damage and a potential third health level of damage here. It makes Blood Lash just shittier than its sorcerous equivalent all around. I think having it require a wound is enough myself, and makes the control spell value really cool.</li> </ul><b>Blood Mirror Speech</b><ul><li>I think you combined our versions here, which is cool, though this does seem to make it superior to Infallible Messenger, especially with the differing costs and the lack of geographic limitation. In my version, I included the linguistics control effect to make it so that it could serve a distinct function alongside Infallible Messenger, though this might seem to just be Infallible Messenger+.</li> <li>I would lower the cost to 5n and increase the wp cost to 2wp. IM has this for a reason, because instantaneous/nigh-instantaneous communication across Creation is actually a pretty huge advantage, so making it draining on a less readily renewable resource is valuable.</li> </ul><b>Bone Puppet Dance</b><ul><li>I suggested edits to this spell on someone else's Abyssal's conversion that clean up the mechanics for 3rd Edition and make it a simpler spell to parse. Will update this post with that.</li> </ul><b>Bonfire Visions</b><ul><li>I like the concept, though this is the kind of thing that seems like thaumaturgy to me.</li> <li>I think, if they still exist conceptually that Fetters are likely mechanically represented through things Ghosts have intimacies towards. I would suggest revising the language to reflect the concept of fetters not as a mechanical term, but a holistic ones referencing the mechanical weight of intimacies. The same might work for the converse.</li> </ul><b>Flesh and Bone Winds</b><ul><li>Very powerful. Reminds me of Cantata of Empty Voices. Not sure if appropriate for a Shadowlands Circle Spell.</li> </ul>I hope some of these thoughts help with the project! I dig the layout so far and am excited to see how it continues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T13:04:30-08:00","id":1040828,"title":"","content":"Is there...like...a sorcery homebrew thread anywhere?<br /> I'm kinda looking for a 3e Food from the Aerial Table, because I find the idea of that as a control spell hilarious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T13:41:24-08:00","id":1040864,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"159\" data-vbnamecard=\"159\">Leetsepeak</a> has done a number of excellent spell conversions in the thread their signature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12025,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12025-praxiscat","user":"PraxisCat","date":".  a word 01-30-2017, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12025-praxiscat","name":"PraxisCat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12025_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T14:43:02-08:00","id":1040908,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all of the feedback. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1037353-the-necromancy-homebrew-thread?p=1040815#post1040815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Three Circles</b><ul><li>Second paragraph states that a necromancer begins by learning Labyrinth Circle Necromancy, when this is not true, they begin by learning Shadowlands Circle Necromancy.</li> <li>I might suggest removing mention of the Liminals here, or possibly giving them access to Labyrinth Circle Necromancy. I believe we've been informed that their level of ability is Terrestrial going on low Celestial in some ways, and if there were any place where they might go further, I would suggest that it be there.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Good find. I will edit immediately. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1037353-the-necromancy-homebrew-thread?p=1040815#post1040815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Banishing Ghosts</b><ul><li>I'm not sure I'd give this as an intrinsic capability. Banishing spells are generally gone and I think that's probably a good thing. It might be worth inquiring around or thinking about why it's strictly necessary for them to have this capability as an intrinsic one, if not as an actual spell.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of a necromancer as someone that ghosts fear. Giving him some level of control over ghosts as default helps emphasize that idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1037353-the-necromancy-homebrew-thread?p=1040815#post1040815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Anointed by Crimson</b><ul><li>While I originally wrote it, the descriptive text of this Initiation definitely needs punching up, IMO. The language is awkward and repetitive.</li> <li>I like that first shaping ritual. Clever way to do it.</li> <li>The second one is crazy good. Although the amount of blood required makes it not super feasible beyond certain levels of usage, but this one is very powerful, and that might be something to look out for. Also what happens if you bathe in the blood of a Size 0 group of people? That is, 1-2 people or a group of sub-size 1 people?</li> <li>The language of this last one should be changed. Rather than saying it lowers the cost, I would say they gain necrosis. I would also describe the nature of the kinds of stunts which would qualify for this shaping ritual.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>I've edited the text a bit. I agree that the second ritual is a bit good, but I'm not sure if it's too good based on how much blood is necessary. I could see myself using it for a bad guy NPC going up against the PCs. Size 1 is the minimum number of people you need to drain, which should also be about the number of people you need to fill a tub. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1037353-the-necromancy-homebrew-thread?p=1040815#post1040815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Schooling of the Maze</b><ul><li>I might suggest rewriting the fluff of this one to cast it as the &quot;Sijanese Initiation&quot; y'know, one involving the Funereal Order.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good idea. I might do that at a later date. Focusing on tweaks tonight. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1037353-the-necromancy-homebrew-thread?p=1040815#post1040815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Black Candle Visage</b><ul><li>This feels exactly like the kind of spell that wouldn't appear in 3e but was in previous editions because we didn't have sorcerous/necromantic workings to use.</li> <li>If you absolutely have to keep it, I would simplify it with the suggestion that it simply allows you to twist normal or mundane ghosts into more monstrous varieties. Like Tiger Warrior Training turning Medium Infantry into Elite Troops, this could turn a Haunt or an Honored Ancestor or a Hungry Ghost or a War Ghost into a Mortwright for example. I'd probably pick a few simple templates of ghostly monstrousness (Or just stick to mortwrights) to facilitate this.</li> <li>I critique the use of the Crafts system here not because I don't like it (I do!) but because I think it's easy to systemize this kind of thing (only 1 dot merits, only 2 dot merits, etc.) to the point of uselessness. If I had to use Crafts with this, I would suggest that minor alterations to the ghost might be minor projects, while severe ones which reshape the form or alter the abilities would be Major. Keeping it simple so that it's easy to use in play.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Some good suggestions. I will keep this in mind and possible rewrite it at a later date. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1037353-the-necromancy-homebrew-thread?p=1040815#post1040815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Bless the Rapine Soul</b><ul><li>Interesting! I like this one. I have a kind of intangible weird feeling about it, but I like it. I think it could use some better word ordering or simplification, hmm.</li> <li>Why the Mute keyword?</li> <li>I think this makes sense as using the default number of necrosis/smotes needed to cast the spell at 15, rather than 10.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>I added the Mute keyword so that the spell could be used without the target knowing it. The idea is that the necromancer manipulates the target into agreeing to be possessed. Increasing the cost makes sense though. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1037353-the-necromancy-homebrew-thread?p=1040815#post1040815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Blessed Dead Fools</b><ul><li>Two bless spells in a row! I'd consider some name fiddling.</li> <li>I appreciate the flavor of this one, but question the necessity of its existence. Since this is a digital work and wordcount isn't a problem, it's less bothersome, but if this were being made to be printed, I would cut this in favor of more useful spells.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I like this one a lot. Also, I blame alphabetical order for the name thing. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1037353-the-necromancy-homebrew-thread?p=1040815#post1040815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Blood Lash</b><ul><li>Cool. I suggest ditching the 2 dot merit for Anointed by Crimson if you want this spell, as that way it isn't a redundancy for the redundant department of redundancy to deal with.</li> <li>I think having people have to reference back to the corebook to figure out what the heck stats their blood lash gets is not a good call. I'd follow the model of Wood Dragon's Claws, which describes the traits of the weapon and what it might be used for inside. the body text.</li> <li>It's interesting that this costs 2wp. WDC costs 1wp and you're getting roughly similar value from them.</li> <li>I caution against having it inflict a second health level of damage and a potential third health level of damage here. It makes Blood Lash just shittier than its sorcerous equivalent all around. I think having it require a wound is enough myself, and makes the control spell value really cool.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>I ditched it. I reduced the cost to 1wp. Keep in mind though that Willpower can be substituted for lethal damage for Blood Magic spells, so technically the Willpower and the required wound could be combined by the necromancer. I also removed the need for the second wound, so the only cost for the spell now is the five necrosis and the intial bleeding wound (that can substitute the Willpower cost). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1037353-the-necromancy-homebrew-thread?p=1040815#post1040815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Blood Mirror Speech</b><ul><li>I think you combined our versions here, which is cool, though this does seem to make it superior to Infallible Messenger, especially with the differing costs and the lack of geographic limitation. In my version, I included the linguistics control effect to make it so that it could serve a distinct function alongside Infallible Messenger, though this might seem to just be Infallible Messenger+.</li> <li>I would lower the cost to 5n and increase the wp cost to 2wp. IM has this for a reason, because instantaneous/nigh-instantaneous communication across Creation is actually a pretty huge advantage, so making it draining on a less readily renewable resource is valuable.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point and something I've considered previously. I run a character with the spell as his control in game, but he's been on the sidelines so much that I haven't really explored the mechanics of it much. He's pulled off a bunch of nasty mirror stuff though that I haven't written down, but that I've waved off as being Second Circle shenanigans. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1037353-the-necromancy-homebrew-thread?p=1040815#post1040815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Bonfire Visions</b><ul><li>I like the concept, though this is the kind of thing that seems like thaumaturgy to me.</li> <li>I think, if they still exist conceptually that Fetters are likely mechanically represented through things Ghosts have intimacies towards. I would suggest revising the language to reflect the concept of fetters not as a mechanical term, but a holistic ones referencing the mechanical weight of intimacies. The same might work for the converse.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually one of my favorite spells. Mainly because I managed to take the most boring spell from 2E Black Treatise and make it interesting. I agree that the actual text needs to be done better though. I'll do that at a later date. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1037353-the-necromancy-homebrew-thread?p=1040815#post1040815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Flesh and Bone Winds</b><ul><li>Very powerful. Reminds me of Cantata of Empty Voices. Not sure if appropriate for a Shadowlands Circle Spell.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>This spell is the one that I've playtested the most since one of my PCs have it as his control spell. We haven't had any issues with it in game yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T18:27:40-08:00","id":1048014,"title":"","content":"<b>UPDATES:</b> <i>February 13, 2017</i><br /> <br /> <b>GENERAL</b><br /> <br /> - Changed the introduction text to remove the copy-pasted stuff from the sorcery rules and only focus on the actual new information.<br /> - Made a box for &quot;New Keywords&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>SHAPING RITUALS</b><br /> <br /> - Added &quot;Sijanese Initiation&quot; as a secondary name to &quot;Schooling of the Maze&quot;. <br /> - Added the Merit &quot;Empathy for the Grieving&quot; to the &quot;Schooling of the Maze&quot; shaping ritual. <br /> <br /> <b>SPELLS</b><br /> <br /> - Added an info box clarifying &quot;Black Candle Visage&quot; and how it works alongside necromantic workings.<br /> - Added the spell &quot;Death Flies Two Sails&quot;. <br /> - Added the spell &quot;Death Inversion Loop&quot;. <br /> - Added the spell &quot;Death Mask&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T12:13:41-07:00","id":1069528,"title":"","content":"<b>UPDATES!<br /> <br /> GENERAL:</b><br /> - Changed a typo in the Shadowlands Circle Necromancy spell that said it required Essence 3 instead of Essence 1.<br /> <u><b>- Added a list of planned stuff to the end of the document. </b></u><br /> <br /> <b>SHAPING RITUALS:</b><br /> - Altered 'The Eye of Darkness' from the 'Taint of the Everliving' to determine Evocation Resonance. <br /> - Added two shaping rituals to 'The Black Feast'.<br /> - Added the Merit 'Vicious Hungry Soul' to 'The Black Feast'.<br /> - Added the Merit 'Haunted Heirloom' to 'The Imbuement of Ancestors'.<br /> <br /> (this completes all current shaping rituals in the document)<br /> <br /> <b>SHADOWLANDS CIRCLE SPELLS:</b><br /> - Added the spell 'Armor of Blood and Bone'.<br /> - Added the spell 'Blade of Blood and Bone'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T22:22:45-07:00","id":1093543,"title":"","content":"For bless the Rapine souls, does the ghost use it's abillity scores or its hosts when controlling?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T04:14:25-07:00","id":1094831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1037353-the-necromancy-homebrew-thread?p=1093543#post1093543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For bless the Rapine souls, does the ghost use it's abillity scores or its hosts when controlling?</div> </div> </div> </div>The necromancer initially makes a social influence action on the target when using the spell. Later when the ghost wants to possess that target, the ghost uses its own dice pools but adds the necromancer's Essence in successes. When it's actually in control of the person, it uses its host's pools for physical actions while it uses its own pools for mental and social actions (save from Appearance). I should clarify this the next time I edit the document.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T15:00:46-07:00","id":1094954,"title":"","content":"Alright, a new version is up with the following changes:<br /> <br /> <br /> GENERAL<br /> <br /> - Added cover art.<br /> - Added table of contents.<br /> - Added art to Page 7.<br /> - Added art to Page 10.<br /> - Added art to Page 16.<br /> - Added art to Page 19-20.<br /> - Added art to Page 24.<br /> <br /> SHAPING RITUALS<br /> <br /> - Changed the 'Mastery of the Dead Universe' Merit from Rating 4 to Rating 5.<br /> - Changed the 'Empathy for the Grieving' Merit from Rating 4 to Rating 3. Also specified that the added die is a non-Charm die. <br /> - Changed the 'Haunted Heirloom' Merit from doing double 9s to double 8s. <br /> <br /> SHADOWLANDS CIRCLE NECROMANCY<br /> <br /> - (Assassin's Fatal Touch) Clarified how distorting the spell affects a necromancer with it as her control spell.<br /> - (Bless the Rapine Soul) Clarified what traits are being used when possessing someone. <br /> - Added the spell 'Door of the Dead'. <br /> - Added the spell 'Drawing Blind Edge'.<br /> - Added the spell 'Dusk Eyes'.<br /> <br /> NECROMANTIC WORKINGS<br /> <br /> - Added general information about necromantic workings.<br /> - Added information about necrotic ambitions. <br /> - Added information about changes to finesse and means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T14:31:14-07:00","id":1096028,"title":"","content":"I had to make another update this early because I added a bunch of additional content. The Hungry Ghost Style conversion is crazy dangerous and will need some revisions, but it's a first draft. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>GENERAL</b><br /> <br /> - Added an info box about 'haunts' on page 19.<br /> - Added art on page 29.<br /> <br /> <b>SHADOWLANDS CIRCLE NECROMANCY</b><br /> <br /> - Added the spell 'Easing the Forsaken Memory'.<br /> - Added the spell 'Emperor's Chains'.<br /> - Added the spell 'Faces of the Dead'.<br /> - Added the spell 'Field of Fell Dreams'.<br /> - Added the spell 'Five Gifts'.<br /> <br /> <b>FIGHTING STYLES OF THE UNDERWORLD</b><br /> <br /> - Started writing on new fighting styles, starting with Hungry Ghost Style.<br /> - Added the 'Necrosis' keyword to martial arts. <br /> - Added the Hungry Ghost Style Charm 'Blood-Scenting Hunger'.<br /> - Added the Hungry Ghost Style Charm 'Leaping Horror Approach'.<br /> - Added the Hungry Ghost Style Charm 'Lunging Phantom Method'.<br /> - Added the Hungry Ghost Style Charm 'Shrouded Claw Attack'.<br /> - Added the Hungry Ghost Style Charm 'Hungry Ghost Form'.<br /> - Added the Hungry Ghost Style Charm 'Consuming Entropy Strike'.<br /> - Added the Hungry Ghost Style Charm 'Blood-Freezing Technique'.<br /> - Added the Hungry Ghost Style Charm 'Power-Reaping Prana'.<br /> - Added the Hungry Ghost Style Charm 'Spell-Smothering Technique'.<br /> - Added the Hungry Ghost Style Charm 'Unnatural Shambling Deftness'.<br /> - Added the Hungry Ghost Style Charm 'Scuttling Apparition Defense'.<br /> - Added the Hungry Ghost Style Charm 'Labyrinth-Walking Prana'.<br /> - Added the Hungry Ghost Style Charm 'Soul-Flaying Strike'.<br /> - Added the Hungry Ghost Style Charm 'Soul-Consuming Transcendence'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T16:49:30-07:00","id":1096109,"title":"","content":"~Can humans learn Hungry Ghost Style charms, provided their necromancers?~ NVM re-read the doc whoops.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T13:44:31-07:00","id":1100204,"title":"","content":"It's kind of awkward to make these update posts since I sort of feel discouraged due to the lack of comments. I've put a lot of effort into this, and I have no idea if people actually like the content or not.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway,<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>GENERAL</b><br /> <br /> - Changed the cover.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>FIGHTING STYLES OF THE UNDERWORLD</b><br /> <br /> - Added info about razor harnesses.<br /> - Added the Dark Messiah Style.<br /> - Added the Dark Messiah Style Charm 'Ravaging Blow'.<br /> - Added the Dark Messiah Style Charm 'Foe-Blinding Jab'.<br /> - Added the Dark Messiah Style Charm 'Inescapable Iron Grip'.<br /> - Added the Dark Messiah Style Charm 'Dead Man's Grasp'.<br /> - Added the Dark Messiah Style Charm 'Dark Messiah Form'.<br /> - Added the Dark Messiah Style Charm 'Bone-Shattering Blow'.<br /> - Added the Dark Messiah Style Charm 'Grievous Agony Attack'.<br /> - Added the Dark Messiah Style Charm 'Illustrative Overkill Technique'.<br /> - Added the Dark Messiah Style Charm 'Lashing Tempest Palm'.<br /> - Added the Dark Messiah Style Charm 'Void Avatar Prana'.<br /> - Added the Laughing Wound Style.<br /> - Added the Laughing Wounds Style Charm 'Sensuous Torment'.<br /> - Added the Laughing Wounds Style Charm 'Kiss of the Whip'.<br /> - Added the Laughing Wounds Style Charm 'Rapture in Chains'.<br /> - Added the Laughing Wounds Style Charm 'Laughing Wounds Form'.<br /> - Added the Laughing Wounds Style Charm 'Instructive Punishment Method'.<br /> - Added the Laughing Wounds Style Charm 'Brand of Obedience'.<br /> - Added the Laughing Wounds Style Charm 'Groveling Penitence Prana'.<br /> - Added the Laughing Wounds Style Charm 'Insatiable Slave Stamina'.<br /> - Added the Laughing Wounds Style Charm 'Ecstatic Tenacity'.<br /> - Added the Laughing Wounds Style Charm 'Ravishing the Unworthy Heart'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T14:27:59-07:00","id":1100217,"title":"","content":"Loving the content but the game I'm using it in hasn't started yet so I've got nothing to say except cool concepts!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T16:05:12-07:00","id":1100240,"title":"","content":"I'm enjoying your content greatly but I'm afraid my rules fu isn't up to useful critiquing. I hope you continue the project to completion since I really love ghosts and arcanoi. Thank you for your work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1546-great-cthulhu","name":"Great Cthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1546_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T16:45:19-07:00","id":1100258,"title":"","content":"Hello! I confess I mostly lurk, but I'm a big fan of this little project and I'll be using the rules at my table if my players ever actually progress the plot a bit (we don't meet near often as I'd like; I blame adulthood). I'll let you know how it goes should we finally get there! I'm no rules expert either, but I could TRY to give you some feedback anyways if I notice anything that looks over our under-powered...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2602-mcleprechaun","name":"McLeprechaun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T15:04:34-07:00","id":1100602,"title":"","content":"I really like this. It will be useful for me (in the next few sessions, ghosts will be pretty important) and I have shown the Laughing Wounds Style to a player and really loves it, and is regreting being a heavy armor fighter... XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T15:55:08-07:00","id":1100623,"title":"","content":"I really appreciate the comments. If any of you decide to playtest any of the spells or MA styles, please let me know what your experiences are. I would like to know what works and what doesn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T18:39:12-07:00","id":1104086,"title":"","content":"This work has been a godsend for the campaign I'm in. Especially the introduction of the martial arts. I love the flavour of Hungry Ghost but it feels a little lackluster in use. Blood-Scenting Hunger doesn't really do much of anything that's useful and has too many charms working off of it with no real incentive to have it running. The form charm itself is also a little awkwardly worded. I feel the intent was to trap the user in the form for its duration, as a sort of blood-fueled frenzy, but it makes no mention of that being the case, even if it is implied (apologies if I am completely off on this). It also highlights one of my major concerns for the style, in that it doesn't really feel like it has an identity of its own. All it really does is provide a mote-generating engine for its charms or spells, but there is no real reason to actually take it. The charms aren't exactly consistent in themeing and there are precious few spells I'd consider using in combat so the only use is to funnel all that necrosis back into the charms.<br /> <br /> I'm not exactly the best when it comes to balance or mechanics though, but my ST is so I'll paste in a couple of her thoughts on it:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#737F8D\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Thoughts from a game design perspective:<br /> - I'm not super thrilled with the structure, little things like having two defence-penalising charms in a row are inelegant and make it feel less cohesive as a martial art.<br /> - The form's too bland for my taste in terms of mechanical identity; the flavour's cool but in practice its big defining strength, rather than something like &quot;I get two turns every round&quot; or &quot;I can counter every attack against me&quot; is &quot;I get lots of motes&quot;, which is blehhh. I'd have reframed it as maybe getting some pool of bloodmurder points that can be spent to enhance the effectiveness of later Hungry Ghost charms or converted into necrosis, though that's a totally off the cuff idea that I haven't thought through at all.<br /> - There's not enough Terrestrial in the style; Unnatural Shambling Deftness especially is something that needs to have a Terrestrial limitation because that's specifically something DBs are meant to be bad at.<br /> - There's a bit too much hanging off Blood-Scenting Prana and not enough that Blood-Scenting Prana does by itself, which is especially painful considering it's a simple activation.<br /> - The non-Terrestrial versions of Leaping Horror Approach are like... yeesh. Outrageously large leaps for really painful costs, it's overpowered and underpowered at the same time in ways that make me all sorts of uncomfortable. Fine for DBs though.<br /> - Spell-Smothering Technique is, uhh, what. Why is a martial art suddenly casting Counterspell. That kind of disconnect is fine for SMAs, but it's going a bit far for a regular MA.<br /> - Soul-Flaying Strike is not a 3e charm. Aggravated damage was all the rage in the past, but it doesn't mean as much these days, so it's a very narrow effect.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Some other thoughts of mine, that are just to point out some possible inconsistencies: Hungry Ghost mentions stunting unarmed to lethal, but doesn't actually have unarmed as a form weapon. And likewise Dark Messiah feels like it should have unarmed as a weapon? It's very fitting but that might be intentional. I also feel as though you could do a lot more with blood magic as an idea, right now there is just blood lash and a couple of spells with the tag but it's just full of potential to do more. <br /> <br /> I know you haven't been getting much critique on this, so I hope this helps!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13571-moonlitseer","name":"MoonlitSeer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T00:05:03-07:00","id":1104187,"title":"","content":"Thank you, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13571-moonlitseer\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13571\" data-vbnamecard=\"13571\">MoonlitSeer</a>. That's the kind of criticism I want and need. Since I have many projects going on at the same time, it may be a while before I go back to the necromancy project next. But I will take your comments into consideration when I touch it up the next time. I'm curious if you have any suggestions of your own for how to further explore the blood magic idea? Are there mainly more blood spells, or some new elements entirely that you want to incorporate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T13:57:39-07:00","id":1104853,"title":"","content":"I don't have anything as of yet, like I said I'm really not the best at mechanics or balancing. Right now I've just been focusing on figuring out evocations to use for my Blood Lash user. Some miscellaneous ideas I can throw out without any care for possible system balance or overlap though in terms of spells could be stuff like using blood to heal (whether it's your own or others, the latter seems more fitting though), some more advanced manipulation outside the lash, maybe even controlling other people's blood? Just some thoughts that came to me as I was typing this.<br /> <br /> As for the keyword itself, I'm not sure what you could do with it aside from what you've already done. I like the idea of being able to use sorcerous motes for those spells, but the character I play won't have any use for that. Being able to substitute lethal damage instead of willpower is very nice and flavourful as well. I think it's in a pretty good spot, all things considered. The real thing is just spells themselves. Moving away from blood stuff even, a lot of it is super niche and only has real use when interacting directly with ghosts. I'm not sure what exactly could be done about that, because it's Necromancy and that's obviously its thing and you don't want to step on Sorcery's toes too much, but unless your game focuses a lot on ghosts and the underworld then most of the spells are kind of pointless. Like I said though, I don't know how much could be done about that that doesn't conflict with other things or goes against lore (I will admit, I'm not the greatest lore buff either, having only gotten into the system within the last year).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13571-moonlitseer","name":"MoonlitSeer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T05:30:16-07:00","id":1105037,"title":"","content":"You should avoid using blood evocations for healing. The main theme of being a blood lash user is that you pay a price for your power. Letting that same power heal your wound negates the price you paid for it.<br /> <br /> As for the spells, the majority of the spells written so far are conversions of spells from previous editions. There are many spells that rely on ghosts. But if you think of the Underworld as an entire world and the ghosts as its inhabitants, then those spells become real scary. Swap the term ghost for human and imagine what the spells would do to the people of Creation. The spells may be restrictive for stories set in Creation, but they are the reason why necromancers are extremely feared in the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":482,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","user":"Ekorren","date":". 06-18-2017, 08:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T12:14:38-07:00","id":1105126,"title":"","content":"You must have misunderstood what I meant. Those were ideas for spells, not evocations I was writing for the blood lash. That said, with it as my control spell I almost never need to use my own blood to form it. An example of the kinds of things I'm messing around with for evocations would be having the lash adapt properties inherent in the blood used to form it (for example, a fire-aspect DB would create a lash of flaming blood, a wood-aspect would adapt the poisonous properties of their blood, etc).<br /> <br /> As for the spells, yes, and that's an important thing to have, but at the same time it shouldn't be the extent of what necromancy can do. Being able to do to the living what you can do to the dead is absolutely terrifying and would be an excellent reason for it to be feared. Since necromancy incorporates the manipulation of flesh and blood as well as ghosts, it's a natural extension of what it can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13571,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13571-moonlitseer","user":"MoonlitSeer","date":". 06-18-2017, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13571-moonlitseer","name":"MoonlitSeer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T07:12:58-07:00","id":1145516,"title":"","content":"I don't like the way this handles countermagic, specifically the one circle higher requirement.<br /> My experience is that historically it's had a negative impact on Dragon-Blooded and God Blooded games where it's going to be rare that there's another Necromancer or a Celestial Circle Sorcerer there to stop you and made it less of an interesting thematic choice and more of a powergaming dick move.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T07:25:18-07:00","id":1145520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1037353-the-necromancy-homebrew-thread?p=1145516#post1145516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like the way this handles countermagic, specifically the one circle higher requirement.<br /> My experience is that historically it's had a negative impact on Dragon-Blooded and God Blooded games where it's going to be rare that there's another Necromancer or a Celestial Circle Sorcerer there to stop you and made it less of an interesting thematic choice and more of a powergaming dick move.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any suggestions for improvements? I'm going to get back to this project when I've finished up the Machineborn source book, so I've been thinking about things to change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T05:16:58-07:00","id":1145761,"title":"","content":"I think you've made Necromancy different enough to Sorcery without it, but if you're married to the idea a penalty is better than complete inability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T16:10:37-08:00","id":1158012,"title":"","content":"I've returned to this project and done some edits. Going to be massively adding content to the PDF in the coming weeks. Please comment if you like where it's going or if you have suggestions for improvements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T16:25:20-08:00","id":1158016,"title":"","content":"Love it so far! I've got a game in the underworld and a game with a necromancer antagonist, so its been very helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T18:04:48-08:00","id":1158043,"title":"","content":"A small bit of feedback: When I suggested making the Rectory of the Maw into the Sijanese Initiation, what I meant was rewriting it so that the flavor of it described how the Sijanese might teach necromancy to people (usually members of the Funereal Order.)<br /> <br /> I realized I'd never actually said that before. My bad!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T18:33:37-08:00","id":1158046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1037353-the-necromancy-homebrew-thread?p=1158043#post1158043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A small bit of feedback: When I suggested making the Rectory of the Maw into the Sijanese Initiation, what I meant was rewriting it so that the flavor of it described how the Sijanese might teach necromancy to people (usually members of the Funereal Order.)<br /> <br /> I realized I'd never actually said that before. My bad!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to review the shaping rituals at some point and add a couple of more, but they aren't an immediate priority. I want to focus on adding more spells and such at the moment. If you want to write the Sijanese Initiation as you imagine it and add it to the book, I'll be happy to take it and give you the proper credit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T00:14:29-08:00","id":1158104,"title":"","content":"Huh. 2 questions. <br /> <br /> On rpg.net, they said on that someone made good homebrew on the white wolf forums on necromancy. Did you get it? <br /> <br /> Also, is there a sorcery version of this thread?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T01:01:58-08:00","id":1158108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1037353-the-necromancy-homebrew-thread?p=1158104#post1158104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On rpg.net, they said on that someone made good homebrew on the white wolf forums on necromancy. Did you get it?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is probably it. I haven't seen any other necromancy homebrew floating around, but I was at it pretty early. This has been around for a while.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1037353-the-necromancy-homebrew-thread?p=1158104#post1158104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, is there a sorcery version of this thread?</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't been writing much sorcery, but <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"159\" data-vbnamecard=\"159\">Leetsepeak</a> has some sorcery stuff in his homebrew thread.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":482,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","user":"Ekorren","date":". 11-17-2017, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T14:31:50-08:00","id":1160015,"title":"","content":"I updated the PDF with several more spells, including necrosurgery rules, necrotic prosthetics, and more Arcanoi.<br /> <br /> Very interested in feedback on the necrosurgery, the Centimanes and the Arcanoi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T17:10:14-08:00","id":1160052,"title":"","content":"Some clarity questions:<br /> Does Bone-Lion's control effect only apply to one lion or to any I summon?<br /> <br /> On the Centamani:<br /> The origin lore is awesome, and I like the overall idea of &quot;ghost&quot; exalts, compared to Abyssals vampiric and Liminals...frankenstien-fleshy exalts.<br /> The story of mass murder by the newly arrived Deathlords is an intreasting one. I'd probably personally put a period between &quot;ghosts who will be the deathlords arrive&quot; and &quot;So powerufl to overturn the Centimane&quot;.<br /> The castes are cool, altough the names...bug me? They feel like specific creatures more than over all type. The anima powers and the effect of their bonfire is neet. And the fetter weakness is an awesome idea.<br /> For Blood Coated weapon, are enemy types like literal species? Like I have my human sword, my horse sword, etc?<br /> Appariation is in here Three times. I suppose it's to save on buying books of arcanos?<br /> All the themes of the books seem instreasting.<br /> Elpias is neat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T19:53:09-08:00","id":1160094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1037353-the-necromancy-homebrew-thread?p=1160015#post1160015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I updated the PDF with several more spells, including necrosurgery rules, necrotic prosthetics, and more Arcanoi.<br /> <br /> Very interested in feedback on the necrosurgery, the Centimanes and the Arcanoi.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Speaking purely from fluff:<br /> <br /> Love the Centimanes, but how do they Exalt? What's the criteria for a ghost to suddenly merge with a dead(er) King of Five Fingers and become the replacement? Also, are they all Neverborn cultists and/or are there a few who really are semi-benevolent rulers of the dead?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T21:53:15-08:00","id":1160122,"title":"","content":"I just wanted to say, Ekorren, that I read this the other day, and I loved it! You did a really good job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/740-anaximander","name":"Anaximander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar740_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T00:13:00-08:00","id":1160143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1037353-the-necromancy-homebrew-thread?p=1160052#post1160052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Bone-Lion's control effect only apply to one lion or to any I summon?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can only have one summoned at the time. I should probably clarify that in the spell description.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1037353-the-necromancy-homebrew-thread?p=1160052#post1160052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Blood Coated weapon, are enemy types like literal species? Like I have my human sword, my horse sword, etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's based on creature type. Human is a creature type.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1037353-the-necromancy-homebrew-thread?p=1160052#post1160052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Appariation is in here Three times. I suppose it's to save on buying books of arcanos?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some overlap is okay. There are a number of meat and potato Arcanoi that I feel should be available in more than one Book.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1037353-the-necromancy-homebrew-thread?p=1160094#post1160094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Love the Centimanes, but how do they Exalt?</div> </div> </div> </div>The condition is based on &quot;potential for greatness&quot; combined with &quot;strong will to exist&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1037353-the-necromancy-homebrew-thread?p=1160094#post1160094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, are they all Neverborn cultists and/or are there a few who really are semi-benevolent rulers of the dead?</div> </div> </div> </div>They all began as cultists but that was thousands of years ago. They are as varied as you want to make them. In my Dawn of the Chosen game, there is an NPC who is a merchant prince ruling over a shadowland trade crossroads. He contains the shadowland and makes deals between the living and the dead. He's a Centimane with a strong code of conduct and wants to make good and honest deals. He's not especially devout to the Neverborn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T04:57:21-08:00","id":1160485,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure the Arcanoi tree performing double duty for the Centamani and the Deathlords is the best idea. Also in general that's a lot of keywords and I'm not convinced they make this easier to read.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T09:16:39-08:00","id":1160529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1037353-the-necromancy-homebrew-thread?p=1160485#post1160485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure the Arcanoi tree performing double duty for the Centamani and the Deathlords is the best idea. Also in general that's a lot of keywords and I'm not convinced they make this easier to read.</div> </div> </div> </div>They keywords can be overhauled. Most of them are part of the same structure: &quot;X can use this&quot; or &quot;X cannot use this.&quot; I deliberately wanted to have the Arcanoi perform double duty because I want to open up the opportunity for Centimane PCs to run the &quot;become a Deathlord&quot; story. That would upgrade some of their Arcanoi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T00:31:29-08:00","id":1161778,"title":"","content":"I just wanted to say that your work is nicely written and fantastically well laid out. It looks outstanding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T08:37:52-08:00","id":1161879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1037353-the-necromancy-homebrew-thread?p=1161778#post1161778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just wanted to say that your work is nicely written and fantastically well laid out. It looks outstanding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. Check out my signature if you want to read more of my stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T21:51:55-08:00","id":1163474,"title":"","content":"Is there a reason Void Circle workings are significantly easier then Solar Circle Workings?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T14:16:55-08:00","id":1163708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1037353-the-necromancy-homebrew-thread?p=1163474#post1163474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a reason Void Circle workings are significantly easier then Solar Circle Workings?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an error. They should be exactly the same. Will edit it and upload a new version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T18:23:17-08:00","id":1170057,"title":"","content":"I've only got about a page's worth of material in there (unless I've forgotten some stuff) but if you could toss a credit somewhere for me as 'Viatos' it'd be pretty cool of you. TPO Wind-Sown Snapdragon. I did the Black Feast's intro and ritual 1, the Flesh-and-Bone Winds, and maybe something else I don't recall. Shattering Void Mirror? Maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","name":"Kingdom of One","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T23:11:36-08:00","id":1170101,"title":"","content":"Of course. I'll fix it in the next update.<br /> <br /> You're credited with the original writeup for Black Feast and Flesh and Bone Winds. Shattering Void was originally written by Leetsepeak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":482,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","user":"Ekorren","date":". 12-31-2017, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T09:09:21-08:00","id":1171541,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar482_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"482\" data-vbnamecard=\"482\">Ekorren</a> , could you detail to me what the Anointed by Crimsom shaping rituals do ? What is a lethal health level &quot;available&quot; to the caster?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T09:18:06-08:00","id":1171543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1037353-the-necromancy-homebrew-thread?p=1171541#post1171541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar482_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"482\" data-vbnamecard=\"482\">Ekorren</a> , could you detail to me what the Anointed by Crimsom shaping rituals do ? What is a lethal health level &quot;available&quot; to the caster?</div> </div> </div> </div>If anyone within range has taken a lethal wound, it becomes &quot;available&quot; to the blood mage. They siphon necrosis from those wounds for their shaping ritual. It can be the blood mage's own wounds, or the wounds of those around her. It could also be a lethal worth of blood carried with her in a bottle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T09:37:46-08:00","id":1171547,"title":"","content":"More practical than I expected, but isn't it a bit strong even with that cap?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T09:44:59-08:00","id":1171552,"title":"","content":"it's relatively easy to get those wounds flowing (though for battlegroups i'd still only count a point of magnitude as 1 necrosis), though for combat the spell won't matter much if you dig into the opposition's flesh.<br /> And you do have to be close enough that you'll be prime and easy target while shaping. No reflexive shaping for that one.<br /> <br /> I think i'll go with it, but one can't use the same level twice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 12-29-2017, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T20:18:28-08:00","id":1171949,"title":"","content":"Fantastic work!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T13:26:24-08:00","id":1172058,"title":"","content":"this thing is great. just the act of reading it has one of my players tempted by the dark side","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2107-wiwuno","name":"Wiwuno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T12:35:51-08:00","id":1172353,"title":"","content":"I am liking it!<br /> <br /> I hadn't had time to do a through reading, but these are some things I've caught up:<br /> <br /> - Control Spell Effects: Some of the spells have very negative control effects mixed with the positive, and some only have positive sideeffects. Is there a reason for that?<br /> - Blade of Bone and Blood - This spell restricts heavy weapons as if they were outright superior weapons (looks like a 2nd ed vestige). I'd drop the restriction to avoid penalizing the character's play style. That leaves the question of what would replace the Control Spell effect, I'd suggest letting the caster add a keyword to a weapon.<br /> - Baneful Sun and Shadow - There are two references to internal penalty (another 2nd ed-ism).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T12:56:37-08:00","id":1172359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1037353-the-necromancy-homebrew-thread?p=1172353#post1172353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am liking it!<br /> <br /> I hadn't had time to do a through reading, but these are some things I've caught up:<br /> <br /> - Control Spell Effects: Some of the spells have very negative control effects mixed with the positive, and some only have positive sideeffects. Is there a reason for that?<br /> - Blade of Bone and Blood - This spell restricts heavy weapons as if they were outright superior weapons (looks like a 2nd ed vestige). I'd drop the restriction to avoid penalizing the character's play style. That leaves the question of what would replace the Control Spell effect, I'd suggest letting the caster add a keyword to a weapon.<br /> - Baneful Sun and Shadow - There are two references to internal penalty (another 2nd ed-ism).</div> </div> </div> </div>About the control spell effects: I don't want to force a negative effect where I don't feel like it would fit. Some effects are very negative, yes, but only in circumstances where it feels very thematic. I'm open to balancing this though in case there are effects that are so negative that it would keep people from picking the spells. <br /> <br /> I'll make some edits to those other spells the next time I'll make an update.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T12:02:25-07:00","id":1206561,"title":"","content":"Massive updates. Much more art. Stuff like that. Feedback appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T12:56:30-07:00","id":1206598,"title":"","content":"Holy fuck the Crow Person with the crimson crescent is awesome. As is the blood water fall/river later on.<br /> Is the Flagellant initiation new?<br /> <br /> The improved surgery section is neat, although I prefer lumping that in with workings. <br /> <br /> I'll have to check the Martial Arts Secrets with the full MAs. Serpent of Many Skins looks intreasting, if only for a non-Lunar skin thief.<br /> I like the Centimane as a concept, and their art...except I kinda wish it was more detailed? Except the Banshee, they all have Nazgul cloaks which moves them a bit out of relatable forms.<br /> <br /> Arcanoi seem to be the same?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T13:04:36-07:00","id":1206602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1037353-the-necromancy-homebrew-thread?p=1206598#post1206598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the Centimane as a concept, and their art...except I kinda wish it was more detailed? Except the Banshee, they all have Nazgul cloaks which moves them a bit out of relatable forms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeeah, that's kind of the problem when you use stock art to fancy up your homebrew. You kind of get to go with the art that is available. It's always fun when you luck out and manage to find a stock piece that fits what you have in mind.<br /> <br /> The flagellant has been there for a couple of months, I think, so &quot;half-new&quot; at least. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T13:11:07-07:00","id":1206606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1037353-the-necromancy-homebrew-thread?p=1206602#post1206602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeeah, that's kind of the problem when you use stock art to fancy up your homebrew. You kind of get to go with the art that is available. It's always fun when you luck out and manage to find a stock piece that fits what you have in mind.<br /> <br /> The flagellant has been there for a couple of months, I think, so &quot;half-new&quot; at least. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> huuuuh. I find it fascinating that lots of bits of Christian/Catholic imagery crop up in abyssal work--the Bishop mainly--because despite Evil Buddhist being an Abyssal trope, a 'pardisal' underworld also works for a sort of after life outside the cycle of incarnation.<br /> Also, as I have a dracula deathlord and a snak themed cult, I eagerly anticapte their sections! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T21:16:39-07:00","id":1206788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1037353-the-necromancy-homebrew-thread?p=1206606#post1206606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, as I have a dracula deathlord and a snak themed cult, I eagerly anticapte their sections! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>My players are on their way to meet He Who Thirsts for the Blood of Many at the moment. He's connected to Grieve, where he is known as the Grand Alchemist and is responsible for their White Elixir. This may not be what the devs have in mind with Grieve in the end, but it has been the story for my campaign for years, so that's what I'm running with. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, here's a spoiler for something I just started working on.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/9g8cL3b.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Edit: I've already updated the PDF with some of this Dragon stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":482,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","user":"Ekorren","date":". 04-14-2018, 02:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T06:02:14-07:00","id":1206861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1037353-the-necromancy-homebrew-thread?p=1160529#post1160529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They keywords can be overhauled. Most of them are part of the same structure: &quot;X can use this&quot; or &quot;X cannot use this.&quot; I deliberately wanted to have the Arcanoi perform double duty because I want to open up the opportunity for Centimane PCs to run the &quot;become a Deathlord&quot; story. That would upgrade some of their Arcanoi.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, but is that a mechanically defined path or more narrative one?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T08:12:04-07:00","id":1206883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1037353-the-necromancy-homebrew-thread?p=1206861#post1206861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yes, but is that a mechanically defined path or more narrative one?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, both are important, but the keywords are mechanically defined. The Deathlord keyword distinguishes Deathlords from other ghosts similar to how Mastery and Terrestrial keywords creates variations within Martial Arts Charms. The Centimane power level is in between, with the option of a mechanical upgrade (i.e. the Deathlord keyword) for storylines where you want to play a Centimane who becomes a Deathlord. The distinctions between different types of Centimanes are defined narratively, but expressed mechanically. I want Banshees to be much better than other Centimanes on spectral-form effects, for example, while I want Ghouls to be much better than other Centimanes on sustainability in Creation and tolerance towards sun and salt, and that is mechanically defined through their Arcanoi. There are ultimately a lot of keywords (and could probably be simplified a bit), but the purpose is to create fun versatility where different ghosts feel different to play.<br /> <br /> Edit: If you check out the Merits page on the Centimane chapter, you'll see the exact details around what you gain from the Deathlord storyline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":482,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","user":"Ekorren","date":". 04-14-2018, 11:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T06:57:51-07:00","id":1211395,"title":"","content":"I seem to remember a control-spell cosmetic change from Silent Master's Pollen but it doesn't seem to be in the current version of the doc. Did it get edited out? I love reading about the cosmetic effects taking something as a control spell has.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T15:45:22-07:00","id":1211594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aretii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1037353-the-necromancy-homebrew-thread?p=1211395#post1211395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seem to remember a control-spell cosmetic change from Silent Master's Pollen but it doesn't seem to be in the current version of the doc. Did it get edited out? I love reading about the cosmetic effects taking something as a control spell has.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have been editing spells on and off while writing, but I haven't changed anything in that spell in particular. I managed to dig up an early version of the document and noticed that it was the same. Not sure about other spells though. I should probably add more cosmetic effects though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T11:55:05-07:00","id":1246003,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the necro, but excellent job!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T13:05:24-07:00","id":1246032,"title":"","content":"Thank you for liking it, but I've removed the first post now because I've quit writing homebrew and no longer want to promote the homebrew I've written before. I would be fine with locking this thread too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T16:05:52-07:00","id":1246092,"title":"","content":"Oooh, before you lock it, I forgot to post my Necromancy homebrew I did as part of the Lunar Castebooks fanproject.<br /> <br /> It's hosted <a href=\"https://archiveofourown.org/works/13926246/chapters/32153325\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> Also, a pull for those who would rather not leave the site.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Touched Beyond Death, the Black Nadir Concordant\u2019s necromantic Initiation<br /> You have braved the Labyrinth through to the very precipice of the Void where the tombs of the Neverborn tilt over that place and state of existential nothingness but are never consumed by it. Summoning your courage you placed your hand on the dead and rotting architecture of one of their broken world-bodies, and felt what it meant to be unliving, yet having no laws written for your cycle of reincarnation. A sacrifice was whispered to you, and you paid it, walking away with power over the dead\u2026 and perhaps a few other marks on your soul.&lt;/p&gt;<br /> <br /> &lt;p&gt;Sidebar: Unlike sorcerous Initiations which have Merits that are purchasable alongside them, necromantic Initiations have flaws. Necromancy is a power drawn from decay and death, not construction and life. Like sorcerous Merits, a necromancer may choose to take none, some, or all of the associated Flaws. Unlike Merits, just like normal Flaws, she does not pay any experience for them, and they grant experience to her when they significantly inconvenience or harm her (Exalted 3e page 167). &lt;/p&gt;<br /> <br /> &lt;p&gt;Shaping Rituals:&lt;br /&gt;<br /> Necromancers who journey through the Underworld and Labyrinth to the precipice of the Void may forever benefit from their mystical connection to their journey through those places.&lt;/p&gt;<br /> <br /> &lt;p&gt;For each day the necromancer spends in a shadowland, they gain 1 sorcerous mote, up to a limit of the Shadowlands Circle necromantic spells they know. These motes may only be spent on necromantic spells of the Shadowlands Circle. Bringing the knowledge of the Void\u2019s most black of arts to Creation hastens the final end to the Neverborn, and they grant the Necromancer these motes directly from their own pools. &lt;/p&gt;<br /> <br /> &lt;p&gt;For each night the necromancer spends in the Labyrinth, they gain 1 sorcerous mote, up to a limit of their Essence, which may be spent on any circle of necromancy. That dark place resonates with the necromancer\u2019s tainted soul, buoying it up with its abundant Essence of death.&lt;/p&gt;<br /> <br /> &lt;p&gt;Finally, each time they look upon the precipice of the Void, usually from Stygia\u2019s safe distance, they may roll their Perception+Occult, gaining sorcerous motes equal to the successes. The visions they see, stolen from beyond the event horizon of Oblivion\u2019s center, grant them insight into their next necromantic spell of any circle. Only one such vision may be kept; looking again releases all the sorcerous motes from the previous observation.&lt;/p&gt;<br /> <br /> &lt;p&gt;Other \u2018Benefits\u2019:&lt;br /&gt;<br /> Cannot Achieve Death (Flaw, Minor) - Just like the Neverborn who facilitated your necromantic initiation, you cannot die, even if you seek its release, so long as it is within your power to do so. Whenever your Incapacitated health level(s) would be filled with lethal or aggravated damage, you must take a crippling injury instead (Exalted 3e page 201). This escapes the limit of having to take multiple levels of damage and the once per story limit. Necromancers with this flaw either quickly gain others to match it, avoid combat, become miraculous healers, or master a combat style that prevents them from taking so much damage in the first place.&lt;/p&gt;<br /> <br /> &lt;p&gt;Whispers (Flaw, Major) - The Neverborn whose body you touched whispered the sacrifice required to gain your necromantic power, but that was just the beginning of their dream-speak directly into your mind. Worse yet, they no longer simply whisper, at times they shout or command, or babble incoherently. Every scene in which you interact with at least one Exalted or a god, the beings who conspired to slay your undead benefactor, you are subject to a social attack that uses any relevant Intimacy of the necromancer\u2019s that the Neverborn can grasp to make a 10 dice social attack to either Persuade the necromancer to kill one of them, Instill the Principle \u201c[This Exalt or god] must die, and quickly\u201d, or to Inspire a killing passion within the necromancer. Many necromancers with this Flaw either devolve into death-loving agents of the Neverborn, intensely dispassionate and disconnected people, or develop impressive mental fortitude.&lt;/p&gt;<br /> <br /> &lt;p&gt;Sunscorched (Flaw, Defining) - Your understanding of ghostly nature and the magic that animates them has boiled over into your very skin. The sun, when it strikes you, attempts to burn away your body, leaving only your soul. Unlike the incorporeal ghosts who experience this as banishment from the material world (see Rolls of Glorious Divinity Volume II page 103), you have an actual body that protests being burned off like morning mist. For each hour you spend out of doors in direct sunlight, you take one level of lethal damage. When fully covered in hat, mask, and other clothing, you reduce this damage to bashing. If indoors, under cloud cover, or being carried around in a fully-concealed box-palanquin during the day, you may pay either 5 motes or 1 willpower to prevent one instance of this damage.&lt;/p&gt;</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T18:30:18-07:00","id":1246144,"title":"","content":"Well that isn't what I was hoping for when I replied. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T20:40:57-07:00","id":1246169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1037353-the-necromancy-homebrew-thread?p=1246144#post1246144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well that isn't what I was hoping for when I replied. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>No worries. I'm still proud of the necromancy homebrew and hope that people will use it in their games. But since I was hired by Onyx Path I can't really promote my homebrew anymore. Technically I could still leave it up since I wrote it long before I signed any contracts, but I felt more comfortable removing it from this thread anyway. The links can still be found on a Google search.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T22:48:33-07:00","id":1246197,"title":"","content":"Just don't wipe it out unless you're explcitly called out to.<br /> <br /> That said, the magic of communication! Information copied isn't information stolen <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So you have no control over that book anymore, mwahahahahah<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T04:30:54-07:00","id":1246595,"title":"","content":"If OP will let you do it up as endorsed but artist-showcase semi-official material I'll buy a copy on DTRPG.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}